; Attribute copy chain (first 21 of 31 LDI)
;
; Part of #R$95FF: the unrolled copy of the attribute bytes of a run of cells, entered in the middle by the JR at
; #R$9634
; whose offset is 2 x (32 - run length). Every LDI copies one attribute from the redraw attribute buffer (#R$C400 +
; index) to the attribute file. The chain goes on at #R$9660, whose last instructions finish the run.
; .
; Hardware: writes the attribute file.
;
; HL Redraw attribute buffer address of the cell
; DE Attribute file address of the cell
; BC Decremented by every LDI (the value is not used)
; O:HL Advanced by the number of LDIs executed
; O:DE Advanced by the number of LDIs executed
@label=CopyAttrChain
c$9636 LDI           ;
 $9638 LDI           ;
 $963A LDI           ;
 $963C LDI           ;
 $963E LDI           ;
 $9640 LDI           ;
 $9642 LDI           ;
 $9644 LDI           ;
 $9646 LDI           ;
 $9648 LDI           ;
 $964A LDI           ;
 $964C LDI           ;
 $964E LDI           ;
 $9650 LDI           ;
 $9652 LDI           ;
 $9654 LDI           ;
 $9656 LDI           ;
 $9658 LDI           ;
 $965A LDI           ;
 $965C LDI           ;
 $965E LDI           ;
